WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.820
Welcome to OmniView Episode 117, Balance News Perspectives.

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.780
Today is July 19th, 2026.

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:10.740
The day's biggest stories from around the world,

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.520
what happened, how different viewpoints frame it,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.380
so you can decide for yourself.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.480
Two US soldiers killed in Jordan

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.120
marked the first American deaths since renewed Iran fighting,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.660
raising stakes for Middle East stability

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.200
and global shipping routes.

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.760
Two American service members died,

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.840
and a third remains missing after an Iranian attack

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.560
on a US base in Jordan.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.140
These deaths represent the first from hostile fire

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.920
since a truce earlier this year.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.960
The United States responded with new air strikes

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.840
targeting Iranian revolutionary guard positions.

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:47.640
The strikes follow eight consecutive nights

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.280
of US operations and Iranian attacks

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.080
reported on targets in Kuwait and Bahrain.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.000
France 24 and Al Jazeera described the sequence

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.220
as the heaviest fighting since February.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.920
The Guardian notes that Iranian leaders

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.560
have warned Washington of further consequences

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.860
while US officials frame the response

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.320
as necessary punishment.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.640
Regional governments are watching whether the exchanges

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.840
remain limited to military sites

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.120
or expand to civilian infrastructure and shipping lanes.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:20.720
Observers will track whether additional US strikes

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.960
target specific Iranian oil export facilities

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:27.760
or whether diplomatic channels reopen in the coming days.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.760
Shifting now to developments in Ukraine,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:34.240
Russian forces launched one of the largest ballistic missile

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.800
attacks on Ukraine's capital in recent months,

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.680
killing at least one person.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.260
President Zelensky described the assault as unusually intense.

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.000
The BBC reports the strike as a direct challenge

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.700
to Ukrainian air defenses.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.380
Ukrainian officials emphasized the attack's scale

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.900
while Russian statements have not detailed specific targets

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:56.760
in this round.

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:00.240
The incident occurs amid broader regional tensions

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:02.500
that already involve multiple powers.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.320
Ukrainian authorities will assess damage to infrastructure

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.860
and report on any further Russian launches in the days ahead.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.680
Next, a story from West Africa shows

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:15.320
how distant conflicts affect daily life.

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.660
Health workers in northern Nigeria

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.000
report more children returning to malnutrition clinics,

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:23.980
attributing the increase to higher food prices

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.380
and reduced aid flows connected to the Iran conflict.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:30.860
The Hindu international notes that local aid groups

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.100
see the effects in states already struggling with poverty.

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.860
The disruptions trace to higher global energy costs

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.420
and shipping delays that raise import bills for staple foods.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.720
Officials in the regions say the trend has accelerated

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:45.840
in recent weeks.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.640
Aid organizations will monitor child nutrition data

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.120
through the summer to determine

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.740
whether additional feeding programs are required.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:57.160
In Southeast Asia, Indonesia has drawn attention

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.620
for its diplomatic choices regarding Iran.

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:03.940
Indonesia, the world's most populous Muslim majority country,

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:07.380
sent only its ambassador rather than a higher level delegation

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.880
to the funeral of Iran's supreme leader.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.620
The choice drew criticism from some former diplomats

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:14.920
as a slight to Tehran.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.500
The South China Morning Post reports that the decision

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:22.020
reflects Jakarta's effort to maintain non-aligned policy

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:24.220
while managing relations with Washington.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.740
Former ambassadors questioned whether US pressure

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.420
influenced the minimal presence.

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.540
Indonesian officials have described the move

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:34.760
as consistent with standard protocol.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.900
Analysts will watch Indonesia's voting positions

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:39.720
at upcoming international meetings

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.540
for signs of any shift in its balancing approach.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:45.420
Turning to business developments in Asia,

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.320
three major Japanese firms are collaborating

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.540
on artificial intelligence development

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.740
that relies on navidia processors.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.320
The partnership aims to strengthen domestic capabilities

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.220
in the sector.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.000
Nikkeh, Asia reports the companies are pooling resources

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:03.400
to build large-scale AI systems.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.060
The effort comes as global competition

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:08.180
in AI hardware intensifies.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:12.100
Industry observers note that access to advanced chips

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:15.040
remains a key constraint for non-US developers.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.160
In the energy sector, Chinese manufacturers have expanded

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.920
their share of the worldwide wind turbine market

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.780
to almost 80%.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.800
The growth reflects both domestic production scale

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.680
and exports to other countries.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:32.760
Nikkeh, Asia, tracks the rise through industry shipment data.

00:04:33.180 --> 00:04:36.140
European and US turbine makers have lost ground

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:38.040
as Chinese costs remain lower.

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.700
Governments outside China are weighing

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.640
how to support their own manufacturers

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.040
while meeting renewable energy targets.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.100
Now, some progress worth knowing about,

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:51.280
Uzbekistan has signed agreements with foreign companies

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.520
to develop solar and wind projects,

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:57.720
marking a shift away from its traditional gas-based power system.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:01.140
The country aims to add several gigawatts

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:03.440
of renewable capacity in the coming years.

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:08.000
Nikkeh, Asia, reports that investors see stable policy support

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.080
and available land as advantages.

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.860
The main complication remains the need

00:05:12.860 --> 00:05:15.440
to upgrade transmission lines to carry power

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.080
from remote sites to cities.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.900
Officials have set targets for renewables

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.420
to reach a larger share of the national mix by 2030.

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.480
To really understand the Nigeria story,

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.520
consider how distant conflicts raise food prices

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:31.400
in places far from the fighting.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.480
Most coverage of Middle East fighting focuses

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:36.220
on direct military moves,

00:05:36.220 --> 00:05:39.500
yet the economic ripple effects on distant food supplies

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.800
receive less attention.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.420
When shipping insurance costs rise

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.840
and certain sea lanes face higher risk,

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.980
freight rates for grain and cooking oil

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.580
increase even for countries far from the fighting.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.320
Nigeria imports a significant share of its staples.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:57.680
Higher global energy prices also raise fertilizer

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.160
and transport costs inside the country.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.580
The same pattern appeared during earlier disruptions

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.400
in the Black Sea and Red Sea,

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.080
where benchmark grain prices moved upward within weeks.

00:06:09.580 --> 00:06:12.120
Knowing this link helps readers separate claims

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.900
about local drought from the measurable contribution

00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:17.120
of conflict-related logistics costs.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.600
One concrete check is to follow monthly reports

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:23.580
from the UN Food and Agriculture Organization

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:26.380
on serial import prices for West Africa

00:06:26.980 --> 00:06:29.180
and compare them with updates on Hormuz

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:30.880
and Red Sea transit data.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.160
If you want to go deeper on the latest US Iran developments,

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:39.200
compare how Al Jazeera and France 24 are covering the story.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.080
Tomorrow, watch for any signs that additional US strikes

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.400
have expanded beyond military targets.

